    <string name="oop_concept">1. Object Oriented Programming</string>
    <string name="oop_desc">OOP is a programming approach based on objects and classes.\n\nThe four main concepts are:\n• Encapsulation\n• Inheritance\n• Polymorphism\n• Abstraction</string>
    <string name="inheritance_concept">2. Inheritance</string>
    <string name="inheritance_desc">Inheritance allows one class to acquire properties and methods of another class.\n\nExample:\nclass Dog extends Animal {\n}</string>
    <string name="polymorphism_concept">3. Polymorphism</string>
    <string name="polymorphism_desc">Polymorphism means one name with many forms.\n\nTypes:\n• Compile-time polymorphism - Method Overloading\n• Runtime polymorphism - Method Overriding</string>
    <string name="encapsulation_concept">4. Encapsulation</string>
    <string name="encapsulation_desc">Encapsulation means wrapping data and methods together inside a class.\n\nIt is commonly achieved using private variables and public getter and setter methods.</string>
    <string name="abstraction_concept">5. Abstraction</string>
    <string name="abstraction_desc">Abstraction means hiding implementation details and showing only essential information.\n\nIt can be achieved using:\n• Abstract classes\n• Interfaces</string>
    <string name="collections_concept">6. Collections</string>
    <string name="collections_desc">Important Java Collections:\n• ArrayList\n• LinkedList\n• HashSet\n• HashMap\n• Stack\n• Queue</string>
